[1m[38;2;255;169;64marmada — one vocabulary for a repo's stack, and the agents working in it[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mUSAGE[0m
  armada <module> <verb> [flags]  [38;2;156;163;175mthe verbs Armada owns[0m
  armada helm                     [38;2;156;163;175menter Helm, the agent you talk to[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mMANIFEST — what a workspace is and how to operate it[0m
  config <scan|verify>  [38;2;156;163;175mreport the evidence, then verify what was written[0m
  init                  [38;2;156;163;175mclaim this workspace: ports, .armada/, setup[0m
  up [<component>]      [38;2;156;163;175mstart this workspace's services; wait until they answer[0m
  down [<component>]    [38;2;156;163;175mstop this workspace's services; keep the port block[0m
  status                [38;2;156;163;175mwhat is running, what is mine, what is stale[0m
  check [<selector>]    [38;2;156;163;175mlint, format and test — the verb a gate calls[0m
  skills [show <name>]  [38;2;156;163;175mwhat this repository knows about itself[0m
  components            [38;2;156;163;175mwhat this repository can be filtered by[0m
  commands              [38;2;156;163;175mthe verbs this repository declares[0m
  clean                 [38;2;156;163;175mrelease what this workspace owns[0m
  <name>                [38;2;156;163;175ma verb this repo declares; manifest commands lists them[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mGUILD — you, portable: voice, skills, hooks, workflows[0m
  init             [38;2;156;163;175mbuild your guild by interviewing you[0m
  project          [38;2;156;163;175mput your guild where Claude Code will read it[0m
  pull             [38;2;156;163;175mbring this machine's guild up to date[0m
  push             [38;2;156;163;175msend local guild changes to the remote[0m
  export           [38;2;156;163;175mwrite the whole guild to one portable file[0m
  import <bundle>  [38;2;156;163;175mrestore a guild from a bundle[0m
  ls               [38;2;156;163;175msee what is in your guild[0m
  show <item>      [38;2;156;163;175mprint one guild file[0m
  edit <item>      [38;2;156;163;175mopen one guild file, validate it, and commit it[0m
  delete <item>    [38;2;156;163;175mremove one thing from your guild, and commit the removal[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mFLEET — the agents you do not talk to: Jobs, worktrees, budgets[0m
  spawn <task>           [38;2;156;163;175mstart an isolated agent Job on a task[0m
  ls                     [38;2;156;163;175mwhat is running, what it has spent, and who needs you[0m
  show <job>             [38;2;156;163;175mone Job in full, and why it needs you[0m
  board <job>            [38;2;156;163;175mtake a Job over yourself: worktree and resume command[0m
  answer <job> <answer>  [38;2;156;163;175mgive a waiting Job your decision; let it continue[0m
  inbox                  [38;2;156;163;175mwhat the fleet needs from you[0m
  pause <job>            [38;2;156;163;175mstop a Job's Drone and keep everything else[0m
  resume <job>           [38;2;156;163;175mstart a paused Job's session again[0m
  reap                   [38;2;156;163;175mend every finished Job and release what they hold[0m
  kill [<job>]           [38;2;156;163;175mend a Job and release everything it owns[0m

[1m[38;2;255;169;64mHELM AND THE BRIDGE — where you talk, and what you watch[0m
  helm    [38;2;156;163;175mthe one agent you talk to: wire the toolbelt, report the launch[0m
